--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party tools invoked by these workflows
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The workflows in this repository orchestrate third-party software that is
downloaded at run time via conda and is NOT redistributed here. Each remains
under its own licence, which is unaffected by the Apache-2.0 licence above.
Notable components include GATK (BSD-3-Clause), Snakemake (MIT), samtools and
bcftools (MIT/Expat), bwa (GPL-3.0), and FACETS (GPL-3.0).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Annotation data sources: licence restrictions that affect commercial use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CADD (Combined Annotation Dependent Depletion) is free for non-commercial use
only. The CADD distribution states that scores are "freely available for all
non-commercial applications" and that commercial applications require a licence,
obtainable from UW CoMotion:

    https://cadd.gs.washington.edu/download
    https://els2.comotion.uw.edu/product/cadd-scores

CADD is enabled in the full configs. For commercial or client work without a CADD
licence, use the *_commercial.yaml configs described in manual/requirements.md.

AlphaMissense (https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphamissense) licenses its code
under Apache-2.0 and its published predictions under CC BY 4.0, which permits
commercial use with attribution. Some mirrors redistribute the predictions under
CC BY-NC-SA; confirm the terms attached to the file you actually download.

Reference data from the Broad Institute resource bundle, gnomAD, and Ensembl each
carry their own terms. None of it is redistributed in this repository.
